{"disposition": "Unaccounted", "excerpt": "- **AUC** (Area Under Curve): probability that the model ranks a random positive above a random negative. 0.5 = random; 1.0 = perfect.\n- AUC is **threshold-independent** — useful when you haven't picked a threshold yet.\n- AUC is **insensitive to class imbalance** — useful for comparing models on imbalanced data.", "excerpt_hash": "95ac3c38537aa140daf1bbe0e701318a4da8a7c759608a7d28e77775cb8f7f40", "heading_path": ["05 - ML Evaluation Metrics", "Classification Metrics", "ROC Curve and AUC"], "knowledge_unit_id": "KU-f01240d613d7f30f", "line_end": 62, "line_start": 60, "source_file_hash": "72af1c3db6d86dc2f93167093465fbd6126cb919742ddb5484666ad31dda8a39", "source_format": "markdown", "source_id": "master-ai:03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "source_path": "03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "unit_type": "list", "verification_status": {"accounting": "pending", "editorial": "pending", "extraction": "machine-segmented", "semantic": "pending", "technical": "pending"}}
{"disposition": "Unaccounted", "excerpt": "But AUC can be misleading on highly imbalanced data; consider PR-AUC (precision-recall AUC) instead.", "excerpt_hash": "0c57d20325ef1372b760f05997341cb2ad0d6c06db09cd87fdf312e75dbdc728", "heading_path": ["05 - ML Evaluation Metrics", "Classification Metrics", "ROC Curve and AUC"], "knowledge_unit_id": "KU-0da7a004ebe49cf7", "line_end": 64, "line_start": 64, "source_file_hash": "72af1c3db6d86dc2f93167093465fbd6126cb919742ddb5484666ad31dda8a39", "source_format": "markdown", "source_id": "master-ai:03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "source_path": "03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "unit_type": "prose", "verification_status": {"accounting": "pending", "editorial": "pending", "extraction": "machine-segmented", "semantic": "pending", "technical": "pending"}}
{"disposition": "Unaccounted", "excerpt": "$$\n\\text{Log Loss} = -\\frac{1}{N} \\sum_i \\left[ y_i \\log \\hat{p}_i + (1 - y_i) \\log(1 - \\hat{p}_i) \\right]\n$$", "excerpt_hash": "6fd6120fa85d7e71c3f56a32e45833ae7651efaf6ff2d7b533f0cc1605fa05f2", "heading_path": ["05 - ML Evaluation Metrics", "Classification Metrics", "Log Loss (Cross-Entropy)"], "knowledge_unit_id": "KU-fbdd87b80f75d745", "line_end": 70, "line_start": 68, "source_file_hash": "72af1c3db6d86dc2f93167093465fbd6126cb919742ddb5484666ad31dda8a39", "source_format": "markdown", "source_id": "master-ai:03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "source_path": "03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "unit_type": "math_block", "verification_status": {"accounting": "pending", "editorial": "pending", "extraction": "machine-segmented", "semantic": "pending", "technical": "pending"}}
{"disposition": "Unaccounted", "excerpt": "Penalizes confident wrong predictions heavily. **The standard loss for classification** ([[02 - Mathematics/Information Theory/15 - Entropy Cross-Entropy KL|cross-entropy]]). Lower is better.", "excerpt_hash": "1dba161bce3e25d2b3f8c4240da7a53f0e46e3c3dbceeb485692351e3d3061ca", "heading_path": ["05 - ML Evaluation Metrics", "Classification Metrics", "Log Loss (Cross-Entropy)"], "knowledge_unit_id": "KU-e06403fac6b03598", "line_end": 72, "line_start": 72, "source_file_hash": "72af1c3db6d86dc2f93167093465fbd6126cb919742ddb5484666ad31dda8a39", "source_format": "markdown", "source_id": "master-ai:03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "source_path": "03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "unit_type": "prose", "verification_status": {"accounting": "pending", "editorial": "pending", "extraction": "machine-segmented", "semantic": "pending", "technical": "pending"}}
