{"disposition": "Unaccounted", "excerpt": "A model is **calibrated** if predicted probabilities match empirical frequencies. If the model says \"80% chance of spam\" 100 times, about 80 should actually be spam.", "excerpt_hash": "5ff80e04174c9b730e4af0fc69678e4ba650ed03d908e88e9bd7c90826adb696", "heading_path": ["05 - ML Evaluation Metrics", "Calibration"], "knowledge_unit_id": "KU-698547ee1346e938", "line_end": 127, "line_start": 127, "source_file_hash": "72af1c3db6d86dc2f93167093465fbd6126cb919742ddb5484666ad31dda8a39", "source_format": "markdown", "source_id": "master-ai:03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "source_path": "03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "unit_type": "prose", "verification_status": {"accounting": "pending", "editorial": "pending", "extraction": "machine-segmented", "semantic": "pending", "technical": "pending"}}
{"disposition": "Unaccounted", "excerpt": "Bin predictions by predicted probability; plot predicted vs. empirical frequency. A calibrated model's curve lies on the diagonal.", "excerpt_hash": "ca913e2c7d1291281dc7751cd3f18db7b15e6e545e6167290dc4c92895639c54", "heading_path": ["05 - ML Evaluation Metrics", "Calibration", "Reliability diagram"], "knowledge_unit_id": "KU-732c2b897c6af276", "line_end": 130, "line_start": 130, "source_file_hash": "72af1c3db6d86dc2f93167093465fbd6126cb919742ddb5484666ad31dda8a39", "source_format": "markdown", "source_id": "master-ai:03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "source_path": "03 - Machine Learning/Evaluation/05 - ML Evaluation Metrics.md", "unit_type": "prose", "verification_status": {"accounting": "pending", "editorial": "pending", "extraction": "machine-segmented", "semantic": "pending", "technical": "pending"}}
